# Default CodeQL false positives configuration for CI pipelines.
# Projects can override this by placing their own .codeql-false-positives in the project root.
#
# Format: SARIF partialFingerprints values, one per line and alone on it. A line is compared whole,
# so a trailing comment makes it a different value and silences nothing. Lines starting with '#'
# are treated as comments and ignored.
#
# The gate (gate.sh) lists every finding it fails on with its `primaryLocationLineHash`, so the
# value can be read from the job log. From a local report:
#   jq '.runs[].results[] | {ruleId, fingerprints: .partialFingerprints}' build/reports/codeql/codeql.sarif
#
# Example:
#   abc123def4567890:1
